(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[22 1 "// The module _ssl (queue 209, PYS22 (a); CPython 3.14.10's Modules/_ssl.c and its clinic file) over Go's"] [23 1 "// crypto/tls: ssl.py runs unchanged on it. A context (_SSLContext) keeps OpenSSL's settings as _ssl.c reads and"] [24 1 "// writes them (options, verify mode and flags, host flags, the protocol bounds, the cipher list, ALPN, the"] [25 1 "// certificate chain and key, the trust store) and makes a tls.Config of them for each connection. An SSL object"] [26 1 "// (_SSLSocket, over a socket or a pair of MemoryBIOs) drives a tls.Conn in a goroutine of its own over an"] [27 1 "// in-memory transport (builtins_ssl_conn.go), so OpenSSL's non-blocking contract (SSL_ERROR_WANT_READ, a"] [28 1 "// handshake resumed by calling again) holds for both. Verification is _ssl's own over Go's x509 (the codes and"] [29 1 "// messages of OpenSSL's X509_verify_cert_error_string), certificates decoded as _decode_certificate does"] [30 1 "// (builtins_ssl_cert.go). What Go's TLS does not have is by design (doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 209\")."] [32 1 "// The constants as CPython 3.14.10 with OpenSSL 3.5 defines them."] [70 2 "// the py_ssl_error codes"] [81 1 "// _ssl.c's line numbers in its error messages (\" (_ssl.c:N)\"), from CPython 3.14.10's source."] [108 1 "// sslReady gives SSLCertVerificationError its two bases (SSLError, ValueError), as egReady does"] [109 1 "// ExceptionGroup's."] [121 1 "// sslError is fill_and_set_sslerror: an exception of type t, its args (code, message), the message"] [122 1 "// \"[LIB: REASON] errstr: verify (_ssl.c:LINE)\" with the parts it has, its reason and library attributes."] [153 1 "// sslPEMLib is OpenSSL's ERR_R_PEM_LIB as _setSSLError reports it."] [158 1 "// ---- the context ----"] [174 30 "// the TLS 1.2-and-below list set_ciphers selected"] [181 35 "// the Python object: an ssl.SSLContext's instance, or the context itself"] [182 35 "// one chain a key type (OpenSSL's SSL_CTX keeps one RSA, one EC ...)"] [192 1 "// sslStoreCert is a certificate of the trust store."] [197 45 "// a fallback root's (x509roots/'s distrust-after)"] [201 46 "// basicConstraints"] [209 46 "// keyUsage's keyCertSign"] [213 2 "// X509_check_ca: a version 1 self-signed certificate is a CA"] [217 1 "// addStore puts a DER certificate in the trust store (once: X509_STORE's hash table)."] [224 11 "// OpenSSL keeps what Go's parser refuses; it cannot anchor Go's verification"] [271 29 "// PY_SSL_MIN_PROTOCOL"] [280 3 "// the subclass's instance made here, so the context knows it (CPython hands the SSLContext itself to the"] [281 3 "// SNI callback and as SSLSocket.context)"] [292 1 "// sslDefaultCiphers is PY_SSL_DEFAULT_CIPHER_STRING."] [295 1 "// tlsVersions is the range of TLS versions the context allows Go: its protocol, its bounds and its OP_NO_*."] [329 1 "// ---- passwords and keys ----"] [331 1 "// sslPassword is a password argument: str, bytes or bytearray (at most PEM_BUFSIZE, 1024 bytes), or a callable"] [332 1 "// called when an encrypted key needs it."] [373 1 "// sslParseKey is a PEM file's first private key, decrypted with the password when it is encrypted."] [382 37 "//nolint: the legacy encryption of OpenSSL's traditional keys"] [421 1 "// ---- the security level (OpenSSL's SSL_CTX_set_security_level) ----"] [423 1 "// sslLevelBits are the security bits each level asks of a key or a signature's digest."] [436 1 "// sslKeyBits is EVP_PKEY_get_security_bits: RSA's by its modulus (BN_security_bits' steps), EC's half its order."] [459 13 "// a key Go reads and OpenSSL rates otherwise (Ed448, ML-DSA): not refused here"] [462 1 "// sslSigBits is X509_get_signature_info's security bits of the certificate's signature digest."] [482 1 "// sslPEMMalformed tells whether a PEM block of the file cannot be decoded (no END line, bad base64): OpenSSL's"] [483 1 "// PEM reader stops there with an error, where Go's pem.Decode skips the block."] [513 16 "// pem.Decode skipped this block for a later one"] [557 3 "// PEM_read_bio's error on a block it cannot decode, met while SSL_CTX_use_certificate_chain_file reads"] [564 2 "// ssl_security_cert at the context's security level: the leaf's key, then the chain's keys (OpenSSL 3.5"] [565 2 "// refuses no signature digest here: a SHA-1 leaf loads at level 2)"] [710 1 "// sslDefaultPaths are OpenSSL's defaults on Linux, as get_default_verify_paths reports them."] [715 1 "// setDefaultVerifyPaths is X509_STORE_set_default_paths: the default file loaded now, the directory looked up"] [716 1 "// at verification; $SSL_CERT_FILE and $SSL_CERT_DIR replace them. When the host has no store (no certificate in"] [717 1 "// the file, no certificate file in the directories: tamago, a bare container), the checkout's x509roots/ bundle"] [718 1 "// (Mozilla's roots, with their distrust-after dates as constraints) takes its place (the user's decision on"] [719 1 "// 209's DECISION 1, (a), 2026-11-05)."] [775 1 "// SSLRoot is a root of the fallback store: its DER and, when it has one, the constraint a chain it anchors must"] [776 1 "// pass (x509roots/fallback/bundle's Root)."] [782 1 "// sslFallbackRoots is the bundle's roots, set by the package arbace/pyssl (over arbace/x509roots/fallback/bundle),"] [783 1 "// which the interpreted runtime loads the first time it is needed (so a run that verifies against the host's store"] [784 1 "// never loads the bundle's forms) and a compiled program links."] [787 1 "// SetSSLFallbackRoots is arbace/pyssl's registration of the bundle."] [790 1 "// SSLDistrustAfter is the bundle's rule for a root with a distrust-after date: every certificate of the chain"] [791 1 "// issued (NotBefore) on or before it."] [803 1 "// sslFallback is the fallback store's roots: the bundle's, or, for tests, $PYI_SSL_FALLBACK_ROOTS's (a PEM file"] [804 1 "// standing in for the bundle, a block's \"Distrust-After: RFC 3339 time\" header its constraint, as the bundle's"] [805 1 "// distrustAfter)."] [833 1 "// sslX509Roots is _ssl._x509roots(), a test function as _test_decode_cert: the fallback store's roots as"] [834 1 "// (subject, distrust-after) pairs, the date None for an unconstrained root (read back from the constraint's"] [835 1 "// message, the bundle keeping no other trace of it)."] [863 1 "// pool is the trust store as Go's verifier takes it: the store's certificates and those of the capath"] [864 1 "// directories (OpenSSL's by-hash lookup: every certificate file of the directory)."] [894 1 "// ---- ciphers ----"] [896 1 "// sslCipher is a cipher suite Go implements, under OpenSSL's name and attributes."] [900 19 "// SSL_CIPHER_get_version"] [902 19 "// OpenSSL's Kx= and Au= words"] [903 19 "// Enc="] [904 19 "// Mac="] [907 21 "// the cipher-string words that select it"] [916 1 "// sslCiphers are Go's TLS 1.0-1.2 suites in OpenSSL's default order."] [966 1 "// sslSelectCiphers evaluates an OpenSSL cipher string over sslCiphers (ssl_cipher_process_rulestr's operators:"] [967 1 "// ':' ',' ' ' separate, '+' joins words, '!' kills, '-' removes, a leading '+' moves to the end, \"@STRENGTH\","] [968 1 "// \"@SECLEVEL=N\", which may follow a word directly: \"DEFAULT@SECLEVEL=1\"); false when no cipher is selected. level"] [969 1 "// is the last \"@SECLEVEL=N\"'s N, -1 without one."] [981 2 "// \"DEFAULT\" counts only as the string's first word (ssl_create_cipher_list replaces it by the default list);"] [982 2 "// a word ends at '@'; a \"@KEYWORD\" ends the item: the rest up to the next separator is skipped, as OpenSSL's"] [983 2 "// rule parser does (\"HIGH@STRENGTH@SECLEVEL=1\" keeps the level)"] [1055 1 "// sslCipherDict is cipher_to_dict."] [1079 1 "// sslCipherTuple is cipher_to_tuple: (name, protocol, bits)."] [1084 1 "// ---- the module ----"] [1357 19 "// set while the string is read, as OpenSSL's rule parser does"] [1411 20 "// Go's TLS has no finite-field DHE: the parameters are read and not used"] [1580 2 "// The OpenSSL API level the port follows (ssl.py and the tests branch on it): 3.5.0, the release CPython"] [1581 2 "// 3.14.10's references ran with; the text says what implements it."] [1622 20 "// Go's crypto/rand needs no seeding"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[201 39] [209 39] [259 53] [273 42] [341 22] [347 49] [349 31] [512 38] [531 53] [540 56] [569 42] [582 40] [630 58] [635 58] [640 26] [651 36] [655 39] [665 35] [686 51] [694 35] [700 33] [722 23] [725 23] [729 32] [737 28] [748 33] [768 58] [807 45] [815 39] [816 45] [851 29] [853 38] [885 48] [985 51] [990 36] [995 41] [1009 56] [1110 41] [1144 24] [1162 24] [1198 106] [1218 88] [1223 88] [1227 90] [1331 23] [1418 29] [1420 38] [1463 30] [1604 28] [1614 29] [1615 36] [1619 32] [1639 33]] :go/trails [[913 113] [934 168] [1549 103] [1564 57] [1575 64]]} (go/file "builtins_ssl.go" :imports [


